  "body": "## What changed\nFour MCP tools so an agent can pick what an operation machines, each write going through the existing undoable commands:\n\n- `list_features {model, kinds?, limit?}`: a model's pickable features in world coordinates - planar faces (normal, facing up/down/side/inclined, area, bounds, the smooth patch it belongs to, each boundary loop outer/hole/open with the edge-chain ids that run it), edge chains (closed, edge count, length, ends, bounds), welded patches and corner vertices. 500 rows per kind by default (`limit` up to 20 000, `truncated` flags a cut).\n- Ids are strings `\"face:0x…\"`, `\"chain:0x…\"`, `\"patch:0x…\"`, `\"vertex:0x…\"` (the geometry-hash ids of `model::features_of`), so a JavaScript client never rounds the 64-bit hash. A loop is picked by passing its chain ids.\n- `set_operation_geometry {operation, picks:[{model,id}]}` -> `SetOperationGeometry`, one undo step. `get_operation_geometry {operation}` reads source, area controls and notes.\n- `set_operation_area {operation, area}` -> `EditOperationParams::with_area` with the op's current params, one undo step; the object replaces all area controls, `{}` resets.\n- Refusals are tool errors: malformed/unknown ids, non-model entities, unknown ops, empty picks, unknown area keys, and a feature kind the op can't take (generation's own refusals, said earlier). None reach the history.\n- New code in `mcp/features.rs`, `mcp/pick.rs`, `mcp/area.rs`; `tools.rs` / `mod.rs` get only the registration lines. `operation::selection_drives_region` widened to `pub(crate)`.\n\nNote: #421 (MCP setup tools) also registers tools in `mcp/tools.rs`; whichever merges second takes a trivial merge of the registration lines.\n\n## Readings\nDebug, M5 Mac: `mcp_pick` 2/2, `mcp` 4/4. `scripts/gate.sh quick` (all camcraft-app suites): 1289 passed, 1 failed - the known main red `setup_stock_source::a_new_block_after_a_flip_starts_from_its_own_stock_and_undoes` (#415). Clippy `-D warnings` clean.\n\n## Pinning tests (`crates/app/tests/mcp_pick.rs`)\n- `a_picked_pocket_floor_loop_generates_verifies_and_undoes` - the done-criterion: an STL 40x40x20 block with a 20x20 blind pocket (floor z 10) is imported, the floor's outer loop (4 chains, ids stable across listings) is picked, generated, verified clean and posted (Fanuc): every X/Y stays within +-8 (4 mm cutter inside the ring), deepest Z exactly 10. Area set and undone; undo restores `{\"model\":\"part\"}`, redo brings the picks back.\n- `bad_picks_are_tool_errors_never_a_panic`\n\n## Not exercised\n`list_features` on a real STEP with curved faces (patch rows empty on this fixture); the Multi-Axis Contour chains-only refusal; accepted (not refused) extra/open boundaries. No GUI change, no posted G-code change (the post in the test is the existing generator and post).\n\nDecisions: `docs/decisions/180-mcp-pick-features.md`.\n\nChangelog: MCP tools to list a model's faces, edge chains and loops with stable ids and to set an operation's picked geometry and area controls (undoable)\n\nFixes #180\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
